      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَظِرِّى فَإِنَّكِ نَاعِلَةُ</span></b>  (M, K) is a prov., meaning
<i>Tread thou upon the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظُرَر</span> [<i>for thou art furnished
with leathern shoes</i> or <i>sandals</i>]: (M:) but the
phrase commonly known is with the unpointed
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ط</span> [i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَطِرِّى</span>: see 4 in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طر</span>]. (M, K.)

